* {{ill|Takenami Site|ja|竹並遺跡|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Yukuhashi|ja|行橋市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Fukuoka Prefecture]]) - Over 1,000 tombs * {{ill|Shiroyama Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|城山横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Fukuchi, Fukuoka|ja|福智町|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - National Historic Site, over 200 tombs * {{ill|Mizumachi Site|ja|水町遺跡|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Nōgata|ja|直方市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - Prefectural Historic Site, over 40 tombs * {{ill|Kozuki Cave Tomb|ja|古月横穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kurate, Fukuoka|ja|鞍手町|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Ishinuki Nagino Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|石貫ナギノ横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Tamana|ja|玉名市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Kumamoto Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Ishinuki Anakanon Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|石貫穴観音横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Tamana, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Nabeta Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|鍋田横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Yamaga, Kumamoto|ja|山鹿市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site, 60 tombs * {{ill|Ōmura Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|大村横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Hitoyoshi|ja|人吉市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site, 27 tombs * {{ill|Yokkaichi Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|四日市横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Usa|ja|宇佐市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Ōita Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, 161 tombs * {{ill|Takio Hyakka Cave Tomb Kofun Cluster|ja|滝尾百穴横穴古墳群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Ōita, Ōita|ja|大分市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Ōita) - Municipal Historic Site, 75 tombs * {{ill|Hasugaike Kofun Cluster|ja|蓮ヶ池横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Miyazaki, Miyazaki|ja|宮崎市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Miyazaki Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site == Related Articles == * [[Kofun period]] * [[Decorated kofun|Decorated Kofun]] == References == <references /> == References == * Nagahara, Keiji (1999). Iwanami Japanese History Dictionary. Iwanami Shoten. * Yokohama History Foundation (2013). History of Cave Tombs. *
