{{afc comment|1=To be clear for both of these articles. Here is the text I pasted on numerous Kofun related articles {{nihongo|{{ill|Corridor-type kofun|lt=Corridor-type kofun|ja|横穴墓|12=draft|12=draft}} {{afc comment|1=Contrast with {{ill|Yokoana-shiki sekishitsu|ja|横穴式石室|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|2=ja|3=横穴式石室|4=zh|5=橫穴式石室|6=ko|7=굴식 돌방무덤|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|12=draft|12=draft}} {{afc comment|1=The category [[:Category:Corridor-type kofun]] was one that I made on enwiki with the erroneous association with {{ill|Yokoana-shiki sekishitsu|ja|横穴式石室|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|2=ja|3=横穴式石室|4=zh|5=橫穴式石室|6=ko|7=굴식 돌방무덤|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|12=draft|12=draft}} {{distinguish|{{ill|Yokoana-shiki sekishitsu|ja|横穴式石室|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|2=ja|3=横穴式石室|4=zh|5=橫穴式石室|6=ko|7=굴식 돌방무덤|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|12=draft|12=draft}}}} |横穴式石室|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|2=ja|3=横穴式石室|4=zh|5=橫穴式石室|6=ko|7=굴식 돌방무덤|yokoana-shiki sekishitsu}}. I find it rather absurd that I did that as it is relatively blatantly wrong, but I did not properly check. I am making a disambiguation page at [[Corridor-type kofun]] that should be imported into wikipedia too, and we should sort out this issue before publishing either article for fear of having [[User:Cewbot]] correct the template to the wrong thing. Maybe just a mass replace of that text to [[Corridor-type kofun]] linking to the disambiguation page so disambiguation page fixer people can determine which one it is going to.[[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 04:24, 30 March 2025 (UTC)}} on enwiki I accidentally conflated Cave tombs and {{ill|Yokoana-shiki sekishitsu|ja|横穴式石室|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|2=ja|3=横穴式石室|4=zh|5=橫穴式石室|6=ko|7=굴식 돌방무덤|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|1=Corridor-Style Stone Chamber|12=draft|12=draft}}s a lot but these are distinct[[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 03:15, 27 February 2025 (UTC)}} s. If this is ever approved as an enwiki article, immediately run a speedy renaming on that category. Likewise check all links already on enwiki because they are ambiguous between the two articles, apparently even in terms of having both kanji in them, idk how I did something so dumb back then[[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 01:42, 15 March 2025 (UTC)}} [[File:Yoshimi Yoshimi-hyakuana 2.JPG|250px|right|thumb|{{ill|Yoshimi Hundred Caves|ja|吉見百穴|12=draft|12=draft}} (November 2010)]] [[File:柏谷横穴群.JPG|right|250px|thumb|{{ill|Kashiya Cave Tombs|ja|柏谷横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} (February 2013)]] '''Cave Tombs''' (横穴墓, Yokōbo/Ouketsubo<ref name="rekihaku">{{Cite web|language=ja|url=https://www.rekihaku.city.yokohama.jp/maibun/qa/detail.php?seq=22|title=Q：横穴墓ってなんて読むのですか?|publisher=Yokohama City Foundation for History and Culture|accessdate=2018-07-28}}</ref>) are burial tombs generally carved into slopes or cliffs, typically measuring around 2 meters in height and extending several meters in depth. These tombs served as burial chambers in ancient East Asia and are most commonly associated with the [[Kofun period]] in Japan, where this burial type emerged and became widely used. == Characteristics == [[File:市ヶ尾横穴墓群B群.JPG|250px|right|thumb|{{ill|Ichigao Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|市ヶ尾横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} B Cluster: Forecourt and entrance.]] [[File:出山横穴墓群 2009.03.21 - panoramio (5).jpg|250px|right|thumb|{{ill|Deyama Graves|ja|出山横穴墓群|ja|出山横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}}: Interior view of the burial chamber.]] [[File:楊谷寺谷戸横穴墓群11号墓.jpg|250px|right|thumb|{{ill|Yōkokuji Valley Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|楊谷寺谷戸横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} Tomb 11: House-shaped chamber.]] [[File:長柄横穴群11号墓棺座.JPG|250px|right|thumb|{{ill|Nagara Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|長柄横穴群|1=Nagara Cave Tomb Cluster|12=draft|12=draft}} Tomb 11: Stone coffin base.]] Yokohama tombs closely resemble [[kofun]] tombs with horizontal stone chambers. They were carved into rock faces, featuring entrances leading to passageways (羨道, sendō), which open into burial chambers (玄室, genshitsu). These tombs typically lack Kofuns but include exceptions. Burial chambers often feature bases for coffins (棺座, kanza) and showcase various ceiling styles, such as house-shaped, dome-shaped, or arch-shaped. Some tombs incorporate forecourts and intermediate rooms between the passageway and chamber.<ref name="#1">{{Cite book|language=ja|author=Keiji Nagahara|editor=Eiichi Ishigami|title=Iwanami Japanese History Dictionary|publisher=Iwanami Shoten|year=1999|isbn=4-00-080093-0}}</ref> In {{ill|Kamakura|ja|鎌倉市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Yokohama tombs feature the distinctive "Kamakura-type" (鎌倉型横穴墓), where burial shelves or smaller inner chambers were carved into the rear walls of burial chambers.<ref name="#2">{{Cite book|language=ja|author=Sakae Ward Historical Committee|title=The History of Sakae|publisher=Sakae Ward Community Promotion Division|year=2013}}</ref> Yokohama tombs are typically found in clusters (横穴墓群, yokohama bokun). The {{ill|Yoshimi Hundred Caves|ja|吉見百穴|12=draft|12=draft}} in {{ill|Yoshimi|ja|吉見町|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Saitama Prefecture|ja|埼玉県|12=draft|12=draft}}, comprises over 200 tombs and is a prominent example designated as a National Historic Site. Some tombs also feature wall carvings and paintings, often categorized as decorative kofun. Colored embellishments have been discovered in regions such as [[Kyushu]], [[Kanto]], and parts of [[Tohoku]]. == Origins and Evolution == Yokohama tombs originated in northern Kyushu around the late 5th century during the Kofun period and subsequently spread across western Japan, including the San'in, Sanyo, Kinki, and Tokai regions by the mid-6th century. By the early 7th century, they had reached the Hokuriku, Kanto, and southern Tohoku regions. The practice peaked around the time of the {{ill|Thin Burial Edict|ja|薄葬令|12=draft|12=draft}} before declining in the late 8th century.<ref name="#1"/> == Name == Yokohama tombs are sometimes called "yokoana kofun" (横穴古墳), but technically the term "kofun" refers to Kofuns, which these tombs lack. They are often grouped under broader definitions of kofun but differ significantly in their construction and purpose.<ref name="rekihaku"/> The term "yokohama tombs" became common in the 1960s, gaining popularity among researchers in eastern Japan, whereas western Japan researchers traditionally referred to them as "yokoana." The term "yokohama" is preferred for consistency.<ref name="rekihaku"/> == Distribution and Notable Cave Tomb Tombs == These tombs are found from Kyushu through San'in, Kinki, Hokuriku, and Tokai, with a high concentration in [[Southern Kantō]]. The northern limit is thought to be in northern [[Miyagi Prefecture]]. Approximately 3,000 examples exist in [[Shizuoka Prefecture]]. === Tōhoku Region === * {{ill|Yamahata Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|山畑横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Ōsaki, Miyagi|ja|大崎市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Miyagi Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, 26 tombs * {{ill|Atagoyama Cave Tombs|ja|愛宕山横穴墓群|ja|愛宕山横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Taihaku-ku, Sendai|ja|太白区|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Sendai|ja|仙台市|12=draft|12=draft}}) * {{ill|Mogasaki Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|茂ヶ崎横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Taihaku-ku, Sendai) - 25 tombs, no longer extant * {{ill|Sōzenji Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|宗禅寺横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Taihaku-ku, Sendai) * {{ill|Kiyotosaku Cave Tomb|ja|清戸迫横穴墓|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Futaba, Fukushima|ja|双葉町|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Fukushima Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, over 300 tombs * {{ill|Izumizaki Cave Tomb|ja|泉崎横穴墓|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Nishishirakawa District|ja|西白河郡|1=Nishishirakawa District, Fukushima|lt=Nishishirakawa District|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Izumizaki, Fukushima|ja|泉崎村|12=draft|12=draft}}) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Nakata Cave Tombs|ja|中田横穴|en|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Iwaki, Fukushima|ja|いわき市|12=draft|12=draft}}) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Hayama Cave Tomb|ja|羽山横穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Minamisōma|ja|南相馬市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukushima Prefecture) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Wada Daibutsu and Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|和田大仏及び横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Sukagawa|ja|須賀川市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukushima Prefecture) - Municipal Historic Site === Kantō Region === * {{ill|Jūgorō-ana Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|十五郎穴横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Hitachinaka, Ibaraki|ja|ひたちなか市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Ibaraki Prefecture]]) - Over 300 tombs * {{ill|Karanogosho Cave Tomb|ja|唐御所横穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Nasukaragawa, Tochigi|ja|那珂川町|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Tochigi Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, part of the Hokōda and Wami Cave Tomb Clusters * {{ill|Nagaoka Hundred Caves|ja|長岡百穴古墳|1=Nagaoka Hundred Caves|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Utsunomiya|ja|宇都宮市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Tochigi Prefecture) - 52 tombs * {{ill|Yoshimi Hundred Caves|ja|吉見百穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Yoshimi, Saitama|ja|吉見町|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Saitama Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, over 200 tombs * {{ill|Kuroiwa Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|黒岩横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Yoshimi, Saitama) - Over 30 tombs * {{ill|Jūrō Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|十郎横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Hatoyama, Saitama|ja|鳩山町|12=draft|12=draft}}, Saitama) - 3 tombs * {{ill|Takinojō Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|滝之城横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Tokorozawa|ja|所沢市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Saitama) - 9 tombs * {{ill|Kitaakitsu Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|北秋津横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Tokorozawa, Saitama) - 8 tombs * {{ill|Bikuniyama Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|比丘尼山横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Higashimatsuyama|ja|東松山市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Saitama) - Over 50 tombs * {{ill|Takane Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|高根横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kumagaya|ja|熊谷市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Saitama) - Municipal Historic Site * {{ill|Nagara Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|長柄横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Nagara, Chiba|ja|長柄町|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Chiba Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, over 300 tombs * {{ill|Deyama Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|出山横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Mitaka, Tokyo|ja|三鷹市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Tokyo]]) - Metropolitan Historic Site, 10 tombs * {{ill|Nakawada Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|中和田横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Tama, Tokyo|ja|多摩市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Tokyo) - 14 tombs * {{ill|Todoroki Ravine Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|谷沢川横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Setagaya|ja|世田谷区|12=draft|12=draft}}, Tokyo) * {{ill|Ekoda Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|荏子田横穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Aoba-ku, Yokohama|ja|青葉区|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Yokohama|ja|横浜市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Kanagawa Prefecture]]) - Municipal Historic Site, 2 tombs * {{ill|Ichigao Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|市ヶ尾横穴古墳群|1=Ichigao Cave Tomb Cluster|12=draft|12=draft}} (Aoba-ku, Yokohama) - Prefectural Historic Site, 19 tombs * {{ill|Itachigawa Basin Rock-Cut Tombs|ja|㹨川流域横穴墓群|ja|㹨川流域横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Kamakura-style tomb concentration) ** {{ill|Matsugasaki Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|松ヶ崎横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kōnan-ku, Yokohama|ja|港南区|12=draft|12=draft}}, Yokohama) - Municipal Historic Site, 8 tombs ** {{ill|Shichisekiyama Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|七石山横穴墓群|ja|七石山横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Sakae-ku, Yokohama|ja|栄区|12=draft|12=draft}}, Yokohama) - Over 100 tombs originally ** {{ill|Miyanomae Tunnel Tomb Cluster|ja|宮ノ前横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Sakae-ku, Yokohama) - 23 tombs ** {{ill|Hikoshigaya Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|ひこしヶ谷横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Sakae-ku, Yokohama) - 12 tombs === Tokai Region === * {{ill|Kashiya Cave Tombs|ja|柏谷横穴群|ja|柏谷横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kannami|ja|函南町|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Shizuoka Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, 106 tombs * {{ill|Kitaema Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|北江間横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Izunokuni|ja|伊豆の国市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Shizuoka) - National Historic Site, 101 tombs * {{ill|E-no-ura Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|江浦横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Numazu|ja|沼津市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Shizuoka) - Prefectural Historic Site, 92 tombs === Hokuriku Region === * {{ill|Hōōzan Cave Tombs||ja|法皇山横穴古墳|ja|法皇山横穴古墳}} ({{ill|Kaga, Ishikawa|ja|加賀市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Ishikawa Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, over 150 tombs === Kinki Region === * {{ill|Takaida Cave Tombs|ja|高井田横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kashiwara, Osaka|ja|柏原市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Osaka Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, over 200 tombs * {{ill|Anfukuji Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|安福寺横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Kashiwara, Osaka) - 32 tombs === Chūgoku Region === * {{ill|Jūōmen Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|十王免横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Matsue|ja|松江市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Shimane Prefecture]]) - 37 tombs * {{ill|Kitsunedani Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|狐谷横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Matsue, Shimane) - 16 tombs * {{ill|Kamikonishi Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|上塩冶横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Izumo, Shimane|ja|出雲市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Shimane) * {{ill|Takatsuku Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|高津久横穴墓群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Chibu, Shimane|ja|知夫村|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Oki District]]) === Kyushu Region === * {{ill|Takenami Site|ja|竹並遺跡|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Yukuhashi|ja|行橋市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Fukuoka Prefecture]]) - Over 1,000 tombs * {{ill|Shiroyama Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|城山横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Fukuchi, Fukuoka|ja|福智町|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - National Historic Site, over 200 tombs * {{ill|Mizumachi Site|ja|水町遺跡|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Nōgata|ja|直方市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - Prefectural Historic Site, over 40 tombs * {{ill|Kozuki Cave Tomb|ja|古月横穴|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kurate, Fukuoka|ja|鞍手町|12=draft|12=draft}}, Fukuoka) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Ishinuki Nagino Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|石貫ナギノ横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Tamana|ja|玉名市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Kumamoto Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Ishinuki Anakanon Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|石貫穴観音横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} (Tamana, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site * {{ill|Nabeta Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|鍋田横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Yamaga, Kumamoto|ja|山鹿市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site, 60 tombs * {{ill|Ōmura Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|大村横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Hitoyoshi|ja|人吉市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Kumamoto) - National Historic Site, 27 tombs * {{ill|Yokkaichi Cave Tomb Cluster|ja|四日市横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Usa|ja|宇佐市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Ōita Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site, 161 tombs * {{ill|Takio Hyakka Cave Tomb Kofun Cluster|ja|滝尾百穴横穴古墳群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Ōita, Ōita|ja|大分市|12=draft|12=draft}}, Ōita) - Municipal Historic Site, 75 tombs * {{ill|Hasugaike Kofun Cluster|ja|蓮ヶ池横穴群|12=draft|12=draft}} ({{ill|Miyazaki, Miyazaki|ja|宮崎市|12=draft|12=draft}}, [[Miyazaki Prefecture]]) - National Historic Site == Related Articles == * [[Kofun period]] * [[Decorated kofun|Decorated Kofun]] == References == <references /> == References == * Nagahara, Keiji (1999). Iwanami Japanese History Dictionary. Iwanami Shoten. * Yokohama History Foundation (2013). History of Cave Tombs. *
